The image conceptually illustrates the dendrimer-like structure of the alpha-D-glucan nanoparticles, referred to as Nano-11, which are derived from phytoglycogen. As described in the PDF, these nanoparticles possess a dense, highly branched internal core, resembling dendrimers. This unique structure is fundamental to their design as vaccine adjuvants, facilitating efficient antigen delivery and activation of dendritic cells through surface modifications.